<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/tarp.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tarp-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tarp.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="765" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="phero-shade"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/appraisal-calculators/">Calculators</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checkup</h1><p class="lede">Appraisal locks in a number. Before you demand it, make sure your file can support the number you want. Twelve questions, a weighted score and a to-do list.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to a New York attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full line-item estimate, not just the summary page."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent, itemized estimate. A one-line contractor bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note when each was taken. Add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ paragraph in the policy conditions and note any timing language."><span>Have you read your policy’s appraisal condition?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and calendar the date with the claim calendar builder."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs (tarps, extraction, board-up) and keep every receipt."><span>Were temporary repairs made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page and any endorsements."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet walls, attics, ceilings and roof decking were inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Read the proprietary lease or bylaws repair section and compare it with the master policy and your HO-6."><span>For a co-op or condo: do you know which policy covers which part?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the settlement gap & fee estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, file it on time and keep a copy."><span>If the carrier asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it filed on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn btn-line btn-sm" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-score" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e4eaf3" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#f26a1b" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you enter leaves your browser.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Questions about accepted coverage and the two itemized estimates carry the most weight, because without them appraisal either can’t start or can’t succeed. Photos, policy deadlines and complete scoping come next. Paperwork items carry the least weight but still matter.</p>
<h2>What a strong file looks like</h2>
<ul><li>Written acceptance of coverage, even partial.</li><li>The carrier’s full line-item estimate and your own.</li><li>Dated photos from right after the loss and of current conditions.</li><li>For co-ops and condos, the lease or bylaws section on who repairs what.</li><li>A calendar of every deadline.</li></ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Worth knowing</b>A low score isn’t a dead end. It’s a list. Most gaps can be closed in a week or two, and closing them often moves the carrier before appraisal is even needed.</div>
<p>Then test the economics with the <a href="/appraisal-calculators/settlement-gap-fee-estimator/">settlement gap &amp; fee estimator</a>, or read the <a href="/appraisal-walkthrough/">appraisal walkthrough</a>.</p>

<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is my answer data saved?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Answers stay in your browser and disappear when you leave the page.</p></div></details><details><summary>What score should I aim for?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Roughly 75 or higher means your documentation is in good shape. Below that, work through the to-do list first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does a high score mean appraisal will work?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. It means your file is organized. The economics and the facts of the loss still decide whether appraisal makes sense.</p></div></details></div>
